WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
Florsheim Monster

00:03.900 --> 00:05.860
Is your shoulder all right?

00:05.860 --> 00:09.100
You looked like you were in pain throughout the entire work shift.

00:09.100 --> 00:12.290
Red is such a bastard.

00:13.290 --> 00:17.700
I told him not to hurt my arms because I need them for work,

00:17.700 --> 00:20.140
but that's all he went for during the fight.

00:21.670 --> 00:24.290
Something keeps smelling like vinegar.

00:25.090 --> 00:26.430
Um, well...

00:26.430 --> 00:28.760
I just started working at a sushi restaurant today, and—

00:28.760 --> 00:30.120
What?

00:30.610 --> 00:34.090
I make sushi rice at a sushi restaurant.

00:34.090 --> 00:36.550
What? I can't hear you.

00:36.550 --> 00:40.430
I make sushi rice at a sushi restaurant!

00:40.430 --> 00:42.560
He made me yell it out about ten times.

00:42.560 --> 00:44.320
What a punk.

00:44.320 --> 00:45.330
You said it.

00:45.330 --> 00:46.990
Red is a punk indeed.

00:49.020 --> 00:51.010
B-Blue?

02:24.540 --> 02:27.260
You guys are from Florsheim, right?

02:28.260 --> 02:29.640
Y-Yes.

02:29.640 --> 02:30.820
How did you know?

02:30.820 --> 02:33.370
Vamp never told you guys about me?

02:33.370 --> 02:34.490
N-No.

02:34.490 --> 02:37.080
We were only recruited just recently.

02:37.080 --> 02:39.990
I used to fight against Florsheim, ya know.

02:39.990 --> 02:41.860
Y-You did?

02:41.860 --> 02:43.440
I used to fight with Red

02:43.440 --> 02:45.540
in a team called "the Weather Fighters."

02:47.000 --> 02:50.350
Back then he went by "Weather Red,"

02:50.350 --> 02:51.850
and I used to go by "Weather Blue."

02:51.850 --> 02:53.790
Weather Red?

02:53.790 --> 02:54.590
This is all new to me.

02:54.590 --> 02:58.170
"Weather Fighters" is a horrible name, now that I think about it.

02:58.170 --> 03:00.270
So basically, Mr. Red was supposed to symbolize "sunny,"

03:00.270 --> 03:02.740
while you symbolize "rainy," then?

03:02.740 --> 03:04.820
Yeah, that was our concept.

03:04.820 --> 03:07.420
I get it now.

03:08.320 --> 03:10.140
Since you said you "used to" be in a team,

03:10.140 --> 03:12.330
does that mean you guys are disbanded now?

03:12.330 --> 03:13.650
Well to be blunt,

03:13.650 --> 03:15.560
Red and I didn't exactly get along.

03:15.560 --> 03:17.780
Isn't that why comedy duos separate all the time?

03:17.780 --> 03:19.110
If you think about it,

03:19.110 --> 03:21.630
comedy duos or Hero teams are all the same.

03:21.630 --> 03:23.450
R-Really?

03:23.450 --> 03:25.330
Well if you want to get down to exact reasons,

03:25.330 --> 03:28.240
it was because Red kept hitting on my Chiaki.

03:28.240 --> 03:30.530
We even got into a fist fight about it,

03:30.530 --> 03:34.210
and it even got to the point of whether to put bros before hos.

03:34.750 --> 03:36.610
In the end, we decided to bury our friendship.

03:36.610 --> 03:39.090
Bury it...?

03:47.880 --> 03:50.860
I'm not cute at all!

03:52.590 --> 03:55.120
So I'll take my coffee black.

03:55.120 --> 03:56.910
Watch me drink it.

03:59.030 --> 03:59.940
Hot, hot!

03:59.940 --> 04:03.940
He uses a straw so not to burn his lips.

04:03.940 --> 04:05.870
He is a doll after all.

04:05.870 --> 04:07.390
You <i>are </i> cute.

04:11.700 --> 04:12.540
What?

04:12.540 --> 04:15.240
That punk Blue's been talking shit?

04:15.740 --> 04:17.190
What a bitch.

04:17.540 --> 04:20.110
More importantly, what's with this stew?

04:20.550 --> 04:21.920
Vamp told us to bring it to Kayoko—

04:21.920 --> 04:24.330
I mean to you, Mr. Red.

04:24.330 --> 04:27.240
We may be neighbors but we're still enemies, you know.

04:27.350 --> 04:28.800
So anyway,

04:28.800 --> 04:30.290
about what Mr. Blue said.

04:30.290 --> 04:31.960
Oh, that's all baloney.

04:31.960 --> 04:35.480
I was the one who went out with Chiaki, and he was the one who tried to hit on her.

04:35.480 --> 04:36.580
Are you sure about that?

04:36.580 --> 04:38.510
Whose words are you going to believe; his or mine?

04:38.510 --> 04:39.490
Um, well...

04:39.490 --> 04:43.030
It's not like it matters who actually went out with her—

04:43.030 --> 04:45.490
I believe you! I 1000% believe you!

04:45.490 --> 04:47.540
Damn, that pisses me off.

04:47.540 --> 04:49.030
Where did you meet Blue?

04:49.030 --> 04:51.070
We met on the train.

04:51.070 --> 04:53.330
Mr. Blue got off at the Musashi-Shinjo station.

04:53.330 --> 04:55.960
So he lives in Shinjo now?

04:55.960 --> 04:58.910
I want you to go to Shinjo right now and find Blue.

04:59.740 --> 05:02.030
I won't be able to rest easy until I bitch at him about this.

05:02.030 --> 05:04.320
Why do <i>we </i> have to do it?

05:04.320 --> 05:08.730
Plus Musashi-Shinjo is an awfully big area to just go and find someone.

05:08.730 --> 05:11.250
Oh yeah, I have Mr. Blue's cell phone number.

05:11.950 --> 05:14.220
Please fight us next time, Mr. Blue.

05:14.220 --> 05:15.650
I'll see if I'm up for it.

05:15.650 --> 05:18.090
Here's my number; keep in touch, okay?

05:18.800 --> 05:19.960
Just a moment, please.

05:19.960 --> 05:20.890
Give it.

05:20.890 --> 05:23.960
I don't know his number, so just give me your phone.

05:23.960 --> 05:24.890
Well,

05:24.890 --> 05:28.070
how about I tell you his number and you can use the phone over there?

05:28.070 --> 05:30.190
I said give it to me!

05:30.190 --> 05:31.460
Okay, okay.

05:31.460 --> 05:34.370
I'll call him right now and hand it over to you once we're connected.

05:36.480 --> 05:39.200
Funny, Mr. Blue's not answering.

05:39.200 --> 05:40.460
Let me see it, damn you!

05:40.460 --> 05:41.200
I'm sorry!

05:41.200 --> 05:43.030
I'm running low on batteries, Mr. Red.

05:43.030 --> 05:45.100
I can't have my phone die on me!

05:45.100 --> 05:47.370
I'm expecting a call from my girlfriend later on...

05:48.150 --> 05:49.440
You lying sack of crap.

05:49.440 --> 05:51.010
You didn't even call him,

05:51.010 --> 05:52.680
and your batteries are full!

05:57.770 --> 05:59.210
Yo.

05:59.210 --> 06:01.960
I didn't think you'd call so soon, monster.

06:01.960 --> 06:04.660
Hi, this is your Red calling.

06:05.160 --> 06:06.490
What? Red?

06:06.490 --> 06:07.790
This is a surprise.

06:07.790 --> 06:08.290
What's up?

06:08.290 --> 06:10.780
You know exactly what's up, you punk bitch!

06:10.780 --> 06:13.190
Why are you telling these monsters a bunch of bull?

06:13.190 --> 06:14.240
What are you talking about?

06:14.240 --> 06:16.460
Chiaki was <i>my </i> girlfriend.

06:14.580 --> 06:16.880
My cell phone balance for this month is running low, too.

06:16.460 --> 06:18.830
You were going out with someone else at the time, remember?

06:19.560 --> 06:22.930
Reason has no place in the game of love, Red.

06:22.930 --> 06:23.890
Oh, wow.

06:23.890 --> 06:26.400
Of course a host would say something like that.

06:26.400 --> 06:27.930
A host?

06:27.930 --> 06:30.410
That's probably why he was on the train at that time.

06:30.410 --> 06:32.010
He was probably getting off work.

06:32.010 --> 06:34.030
Let me make it clear for you:

06:34.030 --> 06:36.110
Chiaki told <i>me </i> that she liked me.

06:36.110 --> 06:37.740
She said she liked me too.

06:37.740 --> 06:39.850
Anyway quit being such a bitch!

06:39.850 --> 06:43.120
There's no point in arguing about a girl who's already married.

06:44.300 --> 06:45.480
Wait.

06:45.480 --> 06:46.430
She got married?

06:46.430 --> 06:47.290
Yeah.

06:47.290 --> 06:49.290
No way, I had no idea.

06:49.290 --> 06:50.180
When was it?

06:51.140 --> 06:53.030
Two years ago? Really?

06:53.830 --> 06:55.560
With the owner of a pub?

06:55.560 --> 06:57.930
You mean that one we used to go to all the time?

06:56.730 --> 06:59.210
This is an unexpected change.

06:57.930 --> 07:01.610
And then they went back to the owner's home in the countryside?

06:59.210 --> 07:00.630
Yeah.

07:04.720 --> 07:07.500
So when's your next break from work?

07:08.810 --> 07:10.250
Let's go drink then.

07:10.250 --> 07:12.860
Sounds like they're friends again.

07:10.250 --> 07:12.860
Me? I'm always free...

07:12.860 --> 07:14.990
My cell phone balance...

07:16.910 --> 07:19.640
Yeah, I know who Chiaki is.

07:19.640 --> 07:23.200
I used to be one of her swimming students.

07:23.800 --> 07:27.380
Try dipping your face underwater now, Vamp.

07:27.380 --> 07:29.690
I think I'm okay for now.

07:30.160 --> 07:33.010
I couldn't swim to save my life back then.

07:33.010 --> 07:38.100
So who did Chiaki <i>really </i> go out with?

07:38.760 --> 07:40.840
She didn't go out with either of them.

07:40.840 --> 07:43.410
They were just causing trouble for her by arguing about it all the time.

07:43.410 --> 07:46.800
I just like both of you as friends.

07:46.800 --> 07:49.050
Yeah, that really takes me back.

07:49.050 --> 07:52.080
I used to really get beaten up back then too.

07:52.080 --> 07:53.990
The Weather Three of the Weather Fighters...

07:53.990 --> 07:55.880
There was Weather Red, Weather Blue,

07:55.880 --> 07:57.530
and Weather Yellow.

07:57.530 --> 07:58.760
Weather Yellow?

07:58.760 --> 08:00.390
There were three of them?

08:00.390 --> 08:02.960
The shocking truth has now been revealed:

08:02.960 --> 08:06.250
Sunred used to be a Sentai Hero!

08:09.700 --> 08:13.470
We must do whatever it takes to achieve world domination.

08:13.470 --> 08:15.320
Even if it means fusing inorganic parts to our monsters

08:15.320 --> 08:17.520
in order to enhance their combat abilities.

08:17.520 --> 08:19.640
The scientific capability of Florsheim has given birth

08:19.640 --> 08:24.020
to a horrible monster in order to help defeat Sunred.

08:24.020 --> 08:26.360
Go forth, Combination-type Monster,

08:26.360 --> 08:28.440
Water Pipe Swallowtail!

08:28.440 --> 08:29.670
Are you all retarded?

08:29.670 --> 08:31.540
You could have used something better to combine,

08:31.540 --> 08:32.640
like a beam rifle or something.

08:32.640 --> 08:36.430
Well it <i>was </i> our first attempt, so we didn't know how it'd turn out.

08:36.430 --> 08:39.490
But a water pipe makes a good blunt weapon you know.

08:39.490 --> 08:42.910
You see criminals use it in police dramas all the time!

08:46.330 --> 08:48.730
General Vamp's Quick Cooking.

08:48.730 --> 08:50.810
Hello, everyone. Vamp here.

08:50.810 --> 08:52.720
We've reached our sixth episode;

08:52.720 --> 08:56.250
let's cook our butts off and make some simple recipes, gentlemen!

08:56.250 --> 08:58.800
Today's menu is simple as always,

08:58.800 --> 08:59.710
even down to its name:

08:59.710 --> 09:02.840
A Simple Cabbage and Pork Belly Casserole.

09:02.840 --> 09:04.580
Here are your ingredients.

09:04.580 --> 09:07.630
First we need about one-fourth of a cabbage,

09:07.630 --> 09:09.770
about 300 grams of pork belly meat,

09:09.770 --> 09:11.430
a slice of butter,

09:11.430 --> 09:13.180
and some salt and pepper.

09:13.180 --> 09:15.100
When you have those ready,

09:15.100 --> 09:16.710
you're set to cook.

09:16.710 --> 09:21.190
Cut the cabbage and the pork as seen on screen.

09:21.190 --> 09:24.650
Sprinkle the pot with water so that the pot doesn't burn.

09:24.650 --> 09:27.810
Around two or three tablespoons should be fine.

09:27.810 --> 09:29.470
Dump the butter into the mix,

09:29.470 --> 09:34.150
and pile the pork and cabbage as much as you want over it,

09:34.150 --> 09:36.670
gradually filling the pot to the top.

09:37.810 --> 09:39.890
Next, put a lid on the pot,

09:39.890 --> 09:43.200
and bring the pot to a boil until the cabbage is fully cooked.

09:43.200 --> 09:44.610
Once the juices from the cabbage come out

09:44.610 --> 09:46.370
and your ingredients start looking like a casserole,

09:46.370 --> 09:49.570
add enough salt and pepper, then...

09:49.570 --> 09:51.360
Voila.

09:51.360 --> 09:54.420
A Simple Cabbage and Pork Belly Casserole.

09:55.350 --> 09:56.770
This is really good!

09:56.770 --> 10:00.110
You can also try adding some lemon extract or soy sauce if you want.

10:00.110 --> 10:03.650
I also recommend putting in some chili oil, if you're a fan of spicy food.

10:03.650 --> 10:06.460
You can also make ramen with the leftovers.

10:13.480 --> 10:15.150
How do you like it, Master Hengel?

10:15.150 --> 10:17.200
A rodeo machine, eh?

10:17.200 --> 10:20.200
This rodeo machine helps correct posture by training the psoas major muscles,

10:20.200 --> 10:22.950
and is also effective in preventing back pain,

10:22.950 --> 10:26.600
but the problem lies with the fact that it is a display model.

10:26.600 --> 10:30.350
Buying for a marked down price won't matter if it breaks down soon after it's bought.

10:30.350 --> 10:32.540
There's a small risk that someone else will buy it before me,

10:32.540 --> 10:37.100
but I still need some time to think it over before making the right decision.

10:37.500 --> 10:38.810
All right.

10:38.810 --> 10:42.250
I'll come back tomorrow to try it out again.

10:44.160 --> 10:46.610
Y-Yes, sir.

10:46.610 --> 10:49.650
General Hengel of Florsheim's West Tokyo Division

10:49.650 --> 10:52.640
has a horrifyingly accurate eye when it comes to analyzing things.

10:56.130 --> 10:58.660
Geez, not again.

10:58.660 --> 11:00.660
Why not?

11:01.530 --> 11:02.860
What was that?

11:02.860 --> 11:05.230
Don't stand in front of me.

11:05.230 --> 11:06.350
Good evening, sir!

11:06.350 --> 11:08.390
Are you new here?

11:10.640 --> 11:12.080
You've still a long way to go.

11:12.080 --> 11:14.230
You want me to snuff this guy, Mr. Rei?

11:14.230 --> 11:16.640
We're not gangsters, you idiot.

11:16.640 --> 11:17.450
I'm sorry!

11:17.450 --> 11:18.750
You're so cute!

11:18.750 --> 11:21.430
Where are you going? Take me with you.

11:21.430 --> 11:23.270
Hop in.

11:23.270 --> 11:25.090
To my place.

11:25.090 --> 11:28.060
Korean barbecue at Ginza, compliments of Mr. Rei.

11:28.060 --> 11:29.970
Thank you for the food, Mr. Rei!
